INT. LUNAR GREENHOUSE - ARTIFICIAL NIGHT

A vast pressurized dome of hydroponic trays under violet grow-lamps. Rows of tomato vines climb strings toward the glass. Beyond the dome, the grey regolith and a hard, bright Earth.

IMOGEN VASQUEZ-LEE (40s, station botanist, rolled sleeves, soil under her nails) kneels between two trays with a pair of pruning shears. She is slight and quick, her hair held by a pencil. ANTON BERGSTROM (50s, systems engineer, thick glasses, a tablet always in hand) stands at the far end checking the irrigation readouts, wearing a sweater with a hole in one elbow.

Both are very tired. Neither says so.

ANTON
Pump three is running hot.

IMOGEN
Tell it to calm down.

ANTON
It doesn't take advice.

IMOGEN
Neither do the tomatoes.

She snips a withered leaf. Drops it in a bucket. Anton taps the tablet. The lamps pulse a half-second slower.

ANTON
That's the fourth flicker today.

IMOGEN
I counted six.

ANTON
You counted the ones I didn't.

She stands, stretches her back, and wanders down the row toward him, trailing a hand through the leaves.

IMOGEN
Do you ever hear them?

ANTON
The plants?

IMOGEN
The stems. When the lamps come on. A kind of ticking.

ANTON
That's the heat.

IMOGEN
I know it's the heat.

They stand a moment in the violet light.

ANTON
Imogen.

IMOGEN
Yes.

ANTON
You've been in here eighteen hours.

IMOGEN
They don't water themselves.

ANTON
Actually, they do. That's my entire job.

She laughs, a short cough of a sound. He nearly smiles.

The lights shudder. Both look up. A distant thud rolls through the dome, a bolt shaken loose in the airlock. The vines sway, then settle. The tablet in Anton's hand goes dark, and so does the row of lamps. For three heartbeats there is only the white wash of Earthlight on the leaves.

IMOGEN (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Don't move.

ANTON
I wasn't going to.

The lamps flare back to life one by one. Imogen exhales. Anton wipes his glasses on the hole in his sweater. They look at each other, then at the trays, and then both go back to work without another word, side by side, snipping and tapping in the purple dark.

ANTON (CONT'D)
Pump three.

IMOGEN
Go.

He crosses to a panel and thumps it with the heel of his hand. A pump coughs. Water begins to run. Imogen reaches out and touches a ripening tomato. It is perfectly, impossibly red.

IMOGEN (CONT'D)
Anton.

ANTON
(from the panel)
Mm.

IMOGEN
Come and see.

He walks over. She plucks the fruit, wipes it on her sleeve, and hands it to him. He looks at it for a long time. Then he takes a bite, and the juice runs down his chin, and neither of them says a word.
